ESP-IDF v5.5.5, components/fatfs: FatFs is built without exFAT
(FF_FS_EXFAT 0), and ESP-IDF has no Kconfig option for it. Most SD cards over
32 GB come formatted exFAT, and would not mount. FatFs's exFAT code is there,
and ESP-IDF's VFS layer already handles it (vfs/vfs_fat.c); this turns it on.
The FAT12/16/32 volumes (/fat, /vimrt) are unaffected.

With exFAT on, ff.c uses FF_USE_LABEL in a C expression, where the
Kconfig option it maps to (CONFIG_FATFS_USE_LABEL) is undefined when off:
it is made 0 or 1.

--- a/src/ffconf.h
+++ b/src/ffconf.h
@@ -52,7 +52,13 @@
 /  (0:Disable or 1:Enable) Also FF_FS_READONLY needs to be 0 to enable this option. */
 
 
-#define FF_USE_LABEL	CONFIG_FATFS_USE_LABEL
+/* esp-vim: 0 or 1 even when the option is off (undefined): exFAT's code uses
+   FF_USE_LABEL in a C expression, not only in #if. */
+#ifdef CONFIG_FATFS_USE_LABEL
+#define FF_USE_LABEL	1
+#else
+#define FF_USE_LABEL	0
+#endif
 /* This option switches volume label functions, f_getlabel() and f_setlabel().
 /  (0:Disable or 1:Enable) */
 
@@ -279,7 +285,9 @@
 /  buffer in the filesystem object (FATFS) is used for the file data transfer. */
 
 
-#define FF_FS_EXFAT		0
+/* esp-vim: exFAT on, for SD cards (most over 32 GB come formatted exFAT).
+   FAT12/16/32 volumes (/fat, /vimrt) are unaffected. */
+#define FF_FS_EXFAT		1
 /* This option switches support for exFAT filesystem. (0:Disable or 1:Enable)
 /  To enable exFAT, also LFN needs to be enabled. (FF_USE_LFN >= 1)
 /  Note that enabling exFAT discards ANSI C (C89) compatibility. */
